5.2. Fuzzy comprehensive evaluation model
5.2.1. Evaluation set
Using the k-means method, each indicator was clustered into the following three classifications: Good, Poor, and Very Poor. As shown in Table 3, Good reflects a nearly optimal state of driver vigilance (i.e., normal non-distracted vigilance). The indicators were classified into Good, Poor, and Very Poor clusters. The proportion of each indicator in different clusters was calculated to obtain the set determination.
