The affiliation matrix of each indicator under different tasks is shown in Fig. 8. The baseline (no distraction) and listening to news have the highest proportion of response time (8a) and accuracy (8b) at the level “Good,” while sending messages has the highest proportion at the level “Very Poor.” For horizontal spread of search (8c), the baseline has the highest proportion of ”Good“ while watching news and sending messages have the highest proportions of ”Very Poor.” For vertical spread of search (8d), 1-back has the highest proportion of “Good” while watching news and sending messages have the highest proportions of “Very Poor”. For road fixation duration time (8e), 1-back and listening to news have the highest proportions of “Good” while watching news and sending messages have the highest proportions of “Very Poor”. For mental workload (8f), listening to news has the highest proportion of ”Good“ while sending messages has the highest proportion of ”Very Poor”.
