The driver vigilance scores while participants were engaged in each distraction task are shown in Table 5. For the no-distraction baseline, the membership degrees of “Good”, “Poor”, and “Very Poor” were 0.609, 0.319, and 0.072, respectively. The comprehensive evaluation vigilance score of the baseline was highest (8.257). For the listening to news task and the 1-back task, the membership degrees of Good were highest, the comprehensive vigilance score of these auditory-cognitive distraction tasks were 8.470, 7.650, respectively. However, for the watching news task and sending messages tasks, the membership degrees for “Very Poor” were highest, and the comprehensive vigilance scores of these visual-manual distraction tasks were 6.257, 5.111, respectively.
